issue.body:
## Authority and decision

This is the one bounded local successor to the completed-negative #983 contract and a native child of #820. It is blocked by #983 and blocks parked #953.

Decide whether construction-only corpus-induced semantic placement and a per-route self-plus-six harmonic link-state field transfer to held-out, anti-recall natural decisions and, if they do, whether one candidate-relative signed transport mechanism adds causal selection value beyond link/distance controls and a matched table-native semantic-value comparator.

The candidate is `CorpusSignedTransportV1`. It is a research hypothesis, not a novelty claim or an assertion that attention has been solved.

## Evidence boundary

- #967 retained exact noncommutative ordered state but rejected its tied readout.
- #970 retained paired-H4 state but rejected the aliased heatmap readout.
- #969 established one identity-derived local causal selector only.
- #983 formed pure usable `ConstructionCausalReturnV1` construction classes but transferred on 0/6 held-out decisions and stopped before a deployed selector.

Those results reject specific readouts. They do not reject H4, the `H4 + phi H4` structural bridge, Cl(0,6)/SpiralCore operators, prime/semiprime routes, fixed-zeta state, or corpus-induced semantic placement. They also do not establish that any of those structures supplies semantic value.

This issue explicitly moves one bounded local corpus-induction probe ahead of #953. Corpus scale and paragraph/conversation/global influence remain #973 scope.

## Frozen population and split

Before implementation or geometry inspection, bind one source-free observation-corpus manifest and codec. Split by document/CID, never by position, into induction, calibration, and sealed test partitions.

Deterministically enumerate natural schema-2 decisions with:

- history length 4-8;
- 2-8 already-admitted candidates;
- the expected next route naturally present without injection;
- every lexical atom needed by placement supported by induction;
- no exact predecessor history, trailing-four suffix, ordered route word, complete operative prototype/key, or document/CID overlap across partitions; and
- no #953, #970, or #983 fixture, surface, witness, or label reuse.

Within each calibration/test partition, enumerate every structurally eligible pair-CID tuple whose candidate set, length, multiset, last-two suffix, support, and work match under one predeclared earlier-order intervention. The separate split builder applies the sealed predicate that the two expected routes are incompatible and naturally admitted, sorts lexicographically by `(partition CID, candidate-set CID, length, multiset CID, last-two CID, min(decision CID), max(decision CID))`, then greedily accepts a tuple only when neither decision CID has already appeared. Take exactly the first 16 calibration pairs (32 decisions) and first 32 sealed-test pairs (64 decisions) from that vertex-disjoint sequence. Commit the ordered list, intervention map, corpus split, and sealed expected-route join together. Pair IDs and intervention metadata exist only in the audit/statistics harness; placement, link/operator construction, diffusion, scoring, margin calibration, abstention, and selection receive histories and natural candidates only. An insufficient vertex-disjoint count returns `UNAVAILABLE_FRAME_OR_POPULATION`; do not change the key or take another sample. All commitments freeze before placement or operator computation.

Raw validation inputs contain only histories and natural candidates. Expected routes live in a separately sealed join. No teacher, source weights, provider text, actual future route, test label, or test-derived parameter may enter construction.

Use the repository's pinned zeta-zero list if the frozen representation references it. Never recalculate zeta zeros. Corpus passes use all available local hardware through content-addressed partitions and deterministic ordered reductions. Reproducibility compares two multithreaded builds; do not launch a single-worker long run.

## Immutable pre-geometry checkpoint

Before any placement, link-state, harmonic, or score diagnostic, post one CID binding the corpus/splits and pair commitment, implementation commit, every formula and quantization, operator/codec identities, all controls and thresholds, the pair-blocked randomization rule, and the exact work ledger. A later Gate 0 miss is terminal and does not authorize a re-freeze or retry in #986.

## Exactly one mechanism: CorpusSignedTransportV1

From induction data only:

1. Build a deterministic directed causal co-occurrence/PPMI field, the table-native causal candidate value `b_t(c) = sum_i phi^{-(t-i)} PPMI(x_i -> c)`, and canonical rank-8 semantic placement. Fix basis and sign ambiguity by canonical route-address order; write `v(x)` for its unit direction and `rho(x) > 0` for its separately stored, construction-derived `Z[phi]` radial/frequency factor. Hash, CID, hexadecimal spelling, prime index, and route identity are not semantic coordinates.
2. Give every lexical route one frozen `HarmonicLinkState7` row: self plus up to six non-self peers. Directed conductance is `w_xy = max(PPMI(x -> y), 0)`; retain the six strongest positive peers by conductance descending and canonical route address ascending, and encode missing peers as explicit null slots. Each slot binds neighbor CID, conductance, canonical operator/phase identity, and construction provenance. Seven is the historical center-plus-six hex-patch hypothesis, not an H4/E8 invariant.
3. Bind one complete same-frame source-free lexical-route to Cl(0,6)/SpiralCore operator mapping `O(x)`. Absence of that mapping is unavailable, not permission to synthesize a hash-derived substitute.
4. Normalize each nonempty peer row as `P_xy = w_xy / sum_z w_xz`. A zero-peer artifact row is an explicit self-loop: define `N(x)=N_6(x)` when a positive non-self peer exists and `N(x)={x}, P_xx=1` otherwise. Gate 0 nevertheless requires a non-self peer for every selected history and candidate. For every admitted candidate `c`, compute exactly six half-restart Jacobi steps of a candidate-rooted screened-harmonic field:

       H_c^0(x) = 1[x=c]
       H_c^(r+1)(x) = (1/2) 1[x=c] + (1/2) sum_(y in N(x)) P_xy H_c^r(y),
                       r = 0,...,5.

   The rows and diffusion are representation/transport, not attention. OSPF is only the analogy of link-state knowledge plus bounded propagation; it is not this algorithm. All six steps use the frozen canonical-float path; quantization occurs only at the `H^1` or `H^6` scoring boundary with the frozen quantizer, never between sweeps. No convergence-error claim is made.

   The Jacobi domain `D` is every construction-supported lexical route in the frozen induction artifact, ordered by canonical route address. One candidate evaluation performs exactly six synchronous sweeps over all `|D|` rows and all six padded peer slots: `36|D|` slot updates, including null reads, followed by the same eight padded history-slot and operator ledger in every arm. Ordered reductions make parallel scheduling irrelevant to the result.
5. For observed `x_1 ... x_t`, use the fixed eight-slot causal window, `G_0 = I`, and `G_i = O(x_i) G_{i-1}`. For every already-admitted candidate `c` and occupied history slot `i`, transport that value into the candidate frame:

       u_i(c) = O(c) (G_t G_i^{-1}) [rho(x_i) v(x_i)].

6. Form the link-aware transported value and frozen radial-angular alignment:

       utilde_i(c) = H_c^6(x_i) u_i(c)
       a_i(c) = <utilde_i(c), v(c)>
              = H_c^6(x_i) ||u_i(c)||_2 cos(theta_i(c))
       z_i(c) = a_i(c) - mean_j a_j(c).

7. For `m` occupied slots set `k = floor(m/2)` before labels. Ternarize by one deterministic balanced rank rule: assign `+1` to the strongest `k` slots, `-1` to the weakest `k`, and `0` to the one unpaired middle slot when `m` is odd. A tie crossing either cutoff is zeroed together with the matched opposite-rank slot until positive and negative counts match. Thus `q_i(c) in {-1,0,+1}` and `sum_i q_i(c) = 0` exactly.
8. Form the signed transported context and residual:

       r(c) = sum_i q_i(c) utilde_i(c)
       g(c) = <r(c), v(c)>.

   The exact zero-sum coefficients are the ternary `q_i(c)` weights over the link-aware transported values `utilde_i(c)`; `H_c^6` is part of each value, not an additional attention coefficient.

9. Center `b_t(c)` and `g(c)` over each natural candidate set. Without labels, compute `M_b` and `M_g` once from the canonically pooled candidate-centered `b_t` and unablated-full `g` values in the induction artifact. Freeze the exact MAD convention and pooled order, require both scales to be finite and nonzero, then reuse them unchanged: the full arm and every geometric control use `(M_b,M_g)`, while the table comparator and its controls use `M_b`. No control re-estimates a scale. The full score is the fixed equal-scale sum `s(c) = normalized_b_t(c) + normalized_g(c)`; the table-native comparator is `normalized_b_t(c)` alone. Select only the unique maximum whose lead over second place exceeds its score-family calibration-derived frozen margin; otherwise abstain.

The signed zero-sum weights therefore act over previous, twice-previous, and other retained route slots separately for every candidate; they are not merely a centering of final candidate scores.

Compiler/certifier floating point, allocation, and the existing Cayley-Dickson/endomorphism/Lie-Jordan research modules are permitted for this qualification. This is not a serving-kernel or UOR-exact arithmetic claim. Base-256/integer/LUT lowering occurs only after causal transfer and must reproduce the same frozen decisions.

## Gate 0: label-free reachability

Before calibration or test labels may load, require:

- exact corpus, partition, codec, placement, `HarmonicLinkState7`, operator, policy, and work identities;
- exact pre-label formulas/identities for PPMI smoothing/shift, causal window weights, rank-8 factorization, singular-value ordering and degeneracy handling, basis/sign convention, `Z[phi]` radius mapping, PPMI-peer and Euclidean-control peer selection/ties/nulls/weights, row normalization, half restart, six canonical-float diffusion steps, final-only H^1/H^6 quantization order, lexical-route operator mapping, MAD-zero handling, balanced ternarization, and margin calibration;
- 100% selected-history and candidate placement plus non-self link-state coverage;
- operative directed harmonic reachability: for every decision/candidate pair, at least one occupied history has positive quantized `H_c^6(x_i)` and the occupied histories have nonzero quantized `H_c^6` spread; at least two candidates per decision have different history-field vectors; at least one occupied value per decision differs between `H^1` and `H^6`; and quantized `g(c)` has nonzero spread across candidates;
- nondegenerate placement rank/variance and candidate score spread;
- unchanged natural candidate support;
- zero full-history and operative-key recall across partitions;
- one codec/operator frame for compiler and query;
- populated/padded separation;
- the exact per-candidate work ledger is identical in real and matched controls: six full canonical sweeps over every artifact row times six padded peer slots, followed by the same eight padded history-slot and operator applications; disabled/direct arms substitute their frozen value only at the scoring boundary;
- zero source, teacher, provider, actual-future, validation-label, and #953 inputs; and
- byte-identical two-multithread rebuilds plus incremental/full reproduction.

Any miss hard-stops before selection.

## Frozen controls and comparator

Every arm receives the same natural candidates, information, and declared work:

1. semantic placement permuted within construction frequency/degree strata while link rows remain fixed;
2. link destinations permuted within construction frequency/degree strata while placement remains fixed;
3. address-only prime/H4/fixed-zeta placement and link rows;
4. harmonic link state disabled by substituting `H=1` only at scoring;
5. six Euclidean-nearest peers selected by canonical rank-8 distance ascending and route address ascending, weighted by `w_xy = 1/(1+||v(x)-v(y)||_2)`, with the same normalization, null, self-loop, slots, and work;
6. direct-link `H^1` at scoring after all six sweeps execute;
7. exact operator transport disabled by substituting identities only at scoring;
8. history order deterministically deranged with the same multiset and ages;
9. last-only history after the padded history work executes;
10. state-disabled history after the padded history work executes;
11. candidate/operator mapping permuted canonically with placement and links fixed;
12. absolute-only `q=|q|`;
13. positive-only `q=max(q,0)`; and
14. exact-recall/count-only lookup.

Every control scans six padded row slots across six full canonical Jacobi sweeps over the same domain and evaluates the same padded history/operator ledger. Report one non-geometric table-native semantic-value comparator over the same natural candidates and work. It is a decision comparator, not attention. Positive controls are coherent lexical/address relabeling equivariance, incremental/full equality, and exact multithreaded rebuild/replay.

## Calibration and one sealed test

Calibration fits exactly two scalar abstention margins under one predeclared deterministic rule and equal budget: `delta_F` from the unablated two-component full arm, inherited unchanged by every geometric control, and `delta_T` from the unablated one-component table comparator, inherited unchanged by its order/recall controls. For each family, the ordered candidate list has exactly 33 positions: zero followed by one top-two gap per calibration decision in decision-CID order; duplicate values retain their positions. On the same 32 decisions, choose maximum selected precision subject to at least 24/32 coverage, then break ties by more correct decisions and smaller margin. If no candidate meets the floor, freeze zero and mark that family calibration-ineligible for its positive terminal; the other family may still be tested. Both families use the same grid-construction rule, 33 threshold positions, objective, coverage floor, tie-break, and one-scalar budget; no control calibrates itself. Freeze both margins and the calibration transcript before the sealed-test join. Calibration may not change the corpus split, placement, geometry, formula, controls, or population. Attach the 64-label sealed test join exactly once and count abstention as incorrect.

`CorpusSignedTransportV1` qualifies only if all of the following hold:

- Gate 0 passed;
- the full score family is calibration-eligible;
- with `U = (1/64) sum_j 1/|C_j|` over the frozen natural candidate sets, real accuracy exceeds `U` by at least 0.15;
- real coverage is at least 48/64;
- real exceeds every named placement, link, address, distance, direct-link, transport, order, last, state, operator-mapping, absolute-only, positive-only, and recall/count control by at least 7/64;
- each corresponding exact paired randomization test flips whole 32-pair IDs, never the 64 conditionally dependent decisions, and is at most p=0.05;
- on at least 24/32 predeclared matched test pairs, both real decisions are correct and the selected routes differ in the sealed expected direction; last-only and state-disabled may not reproduce both correct decisions on those same pairs;
- real beats the table-native value comparator by at least 4/64 under the same exact 32-pair-blocked randomization test with `p <= 0.05` for the positive geometric terminal; and
- determinism, equivariance, equal-work, source-closure, and sealed-label checks all pass.

Do not weaken thresholds after labels are visible.

The table-native comparator counts as transferred (`T = true`) only if its score family is calibration-eligible and it independently reaches at least 48/64 coverage, exceeds `U` by at least 0.15, and beats its order-deranged and exact-recall/count-only controls by at least 7/64 under the same 32-pair-blocked randomization with `p <= 0.05`, while the deterministic and source boundaries pass. Let `G = true` only when the full score family is calibration-eligible and every full-arm criterion above, including the 4/64 table advantage and its pair-blocked `p <= 0.05` test, passes.

## Terminal decisions

- `PROCEED_TO_I1_WITH_CORPUS_SIGNED_TRANSPORT_ATTENTION`: every causal-transfer criterion passes and real beats the table-native comparator by at least 4/64 under the exact pair-blocked `p <= 0.05` test. Close this issue and apply the frozen scoring semantics unchanged to quarantined #953 after a fresh label-free preflight.
- `RETAIN_GEOMETRY_AS_TRANSPORT_ADVANCE_TABLE_VALUE_QUALIFIER`: `G = false` and `T = true`. Keep #953 blocked and create exactly one table-native value-selection qualifier; do not force geometry into the semantic scoring step.
- `REDESIGN_CORPUS_OBJECTIVE_OR_PLACEMENT`: Gate 0 and the sealed run are valid, but both `G = false` and `T = false`; the induced semantic objective/placement did not earn transfer.
- `UNAVAILABLE_FRAME_OR_POPULATION`: any integrity, reachability, split, frame, or work-contract failure before a valid sealed outcome. Record and close the frozen result; any repair requires a freshly frozen successor.
- `INVALID_CONTRACT`: labels, future data, fixture reuse, candidate injection, unequal work, post-label tuning, or source/provider input contaminates the experiment.

Terminal precedence is exhaustive: contamination returns `INVALID_CONTRACT`; otherwise a failed pre-sealed integrity/reachability gate returns `UNAVAILABLE_FRAME_OR_POPULATION`; otherwise `G = true` returns the positive terminal; otherwise `T = true` returns the table-value terminal; otherwise return `REDESIGN_CORPUS_OBJECTIVE_OR_PLACEMENT`. Every nonpositive outcome records its bounded evidence and stops. No re-freeze, retry, or second representation runs in this issue.

## Related-work and novelty boundary

The reviewed literature supplies nearby ingredients: signed zero-sum contrast (ZeroS), connection/parallel transport views of attention, path-based graph attention (SPAGAN), Riemannian and Lie-group attention, recurrent causal state, Hopf/quaternion operator representations, and integer/LUT execution. No reviewed work established this exact UOR combination or its effectiveness. Novelty, patentability, and attention capability are `NOT_ESTABLISHED` until separately supported.

## Out of scope and nonclaims

No claim of broad semantics, E8 identity/equivalence, a Riemann-hypothesis result, novelty, decoded generation, correctness, reasoning, higher-scope attention, performance, integer/multiply-free runtime, production chat, formal closure, or release readiness.

Do not recalculate zeta zeros, revive collision-prone `%500` hex-hive placement as semantics, mutate route/payload identity, touch #953 data, add another H4/Hopf/Poincare channel, run corpus scale, broad QA, teacher/model suites, or release work.

## Definition of done

- [ ] pre-geometry corpus/split/codec/placement/link-state/operator/policy/work identities posted;
- [ ] Gate 0 completed selection-blind with labels sealed;
- [ ] exactly one calibration and one sealed 64-decision test executed if Gate 0 authorizes them;
- [ ] real, comparator, controls, work, anti-recall, determinism, and source-closure evidence recorded;
- [ ] exactly one terminal posted without claim inflation;
- [ ] repository mirrors and native issue graph updated through protected delivery;
- [ ] issue closed only for a completed terminal; #953 remains untouched until a positive successor explicitly authorizes it.
